cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CaptureForge, please cite it as below."
title: "CaptureForge: a general-purpose, organism-agnostic hybridization-capture probe (bait) design pipeline"
abstract: >-
  CaptureForge is a reusable, end-to-end Nextflow (DSL2) pipeline that turns a
  gene list plus per-gene design intent into order-ready biotinylated-bait oligo
  sequences and a full QC/design report. It is disease- and organism-agnostic:
  any gene list and (where feasible) any reference genome are supported by
  changing inputs and config only, with no code edits. It sits at the head of the
  forge family and hands its covered-target BED and per-gene metadata to CallForge.
authors:
  - family-names: "Adu"
    given-names: "Bright"
    alias: "aduton1000"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3622-2137"
    affiliation: "Genomics & Bioinformatics Core, Noguchi Memorial Institute for Medical Research, University of Ghana, Legon, Ghana"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-13"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/aduton1000/captureforge"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - hybridization capture
  - bait design
  - probe design
  - targeted sequencing
  - nextflow
references:
  - type: software
    title: "CallForge: a targeted-capture germline analysis pipeline"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/aduton1000/callforge"
    notes: "Downstream analysis pipeline; consumes CaptureForge's final_covered_targets.bed and per-gene metadata."
